# Artist Usability Rules

## Non-Programmer Design
The artist is NOT a programmer. All tools must be usable without:
- Terminal/command line knowledge
- Python knowledge
- Understanding of file paths or arguments

## .bat Launchers
- Every common operation must have a `.bat` launcher in `launchers/`
- Launchers must show clear Vietnamese messages
- Launchers must pause before closing (so the artist can read output)
- Launchers must handle errors gracefully (no cryptic stack traces)
- Launcher naming: numbered for suggested order (01_, 02_, 03_, ...)

## Folder Convention
- `drops/` — Artist drops files here for processing
- `outputs/` — Artist finds results here
- These two folders are the artist's primary interaction points
- Keep the mental model simple: DROP → RUN → GET OUTPUT

## Vietnamese Instructions
- All artist-facing docs in Vietnamese (files ending in `_VI.md`)
- Error messages shown to artist must include Vietnamese text
- Use clear, non-technical language
- Include screenshots or diagrams where helpful

## Non-Destructive
- NEVER overwrite files in `drops/` — process and move/copy
- NEVER delete artist's source files
- If an output already exists, create a new version (never overwrite)
- Show clear message: "File đã được xử lý. Kết quả ở: outputs/..."

## Error Handling
- Show Vietnamese error message to the artist
- Log English technical details to a log file
- Suggest a fix or next step in the error message
- Never show raw Python tracebacks to the artist
